<title>FRANCE: CNA sets 2.2 billion franc 2007 bond.</title>
<headline>CNA sets 2.2 billion franc 2007 bond.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced</p>
<p>by lead managers Caisse Nationale de Credit Agricole and Societe</p>
<p>Generale.</p>
<p>BORROWER - CAISSE NATIONALE DES AUTOROUTES</p>
<p> AMT   2.2 BLN FRF	COUPON     6.30	MATURITY 07.OCT.07</p>
<p> TYPE  STRAIGHT	   ISS PRICE  100.90    PAY DATE 07.OCT.96</p>
<p>				REOFFER    99.95     ACCRUAL  07.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  130 BP	YLD/SPREAD 8 BP</p>
<p>NOTE - Yield spread calculated over interpolated 6.50 percent 2006 OAT and 8.50 percent 2008 OAT. CNA also launched 500 million franc 6.70 percent 2011 issue designed to be fungible with existing 2011 bond, yielding nine basis points over OATs at the reoffer price.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
